WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.9 · Theory of Change
Test, write and use your Theory of Change

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your Theory of Change is useful when people can read it, question it and decide with it.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.504
Your Theory of Change is useful when people can read it, question it and use it to decide. For each pathway, you write a one-page narrative in plain language, test it and keep it up to date.

4
00:00:28.904 --> 00:00:29.504
Write, test, review

5
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:41.574
Write it: One page: the problem, the change, the main steps, key assumptions and their evidence. For example: Our bakery explains in five short paragraphs how paid traineeships lead to first jobs.

6
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:54.015
Test it: Ask future participants, people in the field, partners and one sceptic where it is weakest. For example: A youth-centre manager doubts six months is enough, so the founders add follow-up calls.

7
00:00:54.015 --> 00:01:07.656
Version and review: Give it a version number and a date; review after your pilot, then yearly. For example: Version 0.1, March: a draft before the pilot, to review once the first trainees finish.

8
00:01:08.056 --> 00:01:08.656
Why it matters

9
00:01:08.656 --> 00:01:13.959
1. Plain words help co-founders, partners and funders follow your idea.

10
00:01:13.959 --> 00:01:18.522
2. A sceptic finds weak links before reality does.

11
00:01:18.522 --> 00:01:24.085
3. Versions show how your thinking improved with evidence.

12
00:01:24.485 --> 00:01:25.085
What it feeds

13
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:29.278
1. Your indicators and learning in Module 6.

14
00:01:29.278 --> 00:01:34.581
2. How you present your idea to funders, customers and partners.

15
00:01:34.581 --> 00:01:39.774
3. Your first-year priorities and what you postpone.

16
00:01:40.174 --> 00:01:40.774
What to avoid

17
00:01:40.774 --> 00:01:45.337
A diagram nobody outside the team can read.

18
00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:50.270
Testing only with friends who already agree with you.

19
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.833
Never reviewing it, even after an assumption fails.

20
00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:58.233
You write your test plan, version and review dates.

21
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:02.233
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:06.833
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
